{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_1418470079#1_2870981458","relevance":2,"reason":"The full article confirms a prior watermelon shortage and high prices, and gives causal support that parts of the Southwest started late because of weather problems, causing delayed output. However, the article is mainly about a later oversupply and cheap Texas watermelons, not dedicated to explaining why there was a shortage.","learned":"The strongest evidence so far is that weather problems caused late starts in some Southwest producing areas, contributing to an early-season watermelon shortage before output later surged."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ watermelon shortage (+ australia queensland) (+ flood floods rain weather crop harvest))","reason":"Try a regional search for Australia/Queensland, where fruit shortages are often caused by floods or heavy rain, to find more direct articles explaining a watermelon shortage."}}
