{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_547171863#0_1274523889","relevance":1,"reason":"The passage explains that watermelon is more expensive and lower quality out of season because seasonal produce is cheaper and more abundant, but it is a general seasonal-eating article and not dedicated to an actual watermelon shortage.","learned":"A general cause of watermelon scarcity or higher prices can be seasonality: watermelon is most abundant and best in summer, while out-of-season watermelon is more expensive and often shipped from farther away."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ watermelon (+ shortage shortages scarce scarcity) (+ \"in season\" seasonal seasonality summer winter) (+ supply expensive prices))","reason":"Search for sources that more directly connect watermelon scarcity or shortage to seasonality and supply/prices, since specific weather-shortage searches yielded little and seasonal supply is a plausible general answer."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ watermelon (+ shortage shortages scarce scarcity) (+ \"in season\" seasonal seasonality summer winter) (+ supply expensive prices))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_55_529377695#11_1211773180","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q2809","rank":2,"snippet":"impact can’t be overstated. Our Newsletter \" , \"segment\": \"People were curious about Claws and boom: the following summer was a lawless smorgasbord of ever-so-slightly flavored booze-filled seltzers. Truly and other brands continued to try to compete, and did see success, but none will ever reach the level of notoriety of White Claw. Bros, basic bitches, wine moms, party dads, and college kids alike have all agreed: White Claw is the one. Everyone spent the <cover>summer of 2019 drinking it like it was going out of style, unknowingly threatening their supply. By September of that year, there was a shortage, which was a huge bummer, but didn’t last too long. Fast forward to March 2020, when the pandemic ended the party. But White Claw returned with even more flavors, including lemon, tangerine, and watermelon. </cover>Who knew booze would be what put seltzer on the map?\" , \"start_char\": 4740.000000 , \"title\": \"History of White Claw: How Did 'White Claw' Start? - Thrillist\" , \"url\": \"https://www.thrillist.com/news/nation/history-of-white-claw\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_56_366358143#9_763370298","rank":1,"relevance":1}]}}
